        <page name="tools/contiguouscache" href="qtcore-tools-contiguouscache-example.html" status="active" location="contiguouscache.qdoc" filepath="/home/qt/work/qt/tqtc-qt5/qtbase/examples/corelib/tools/doc/src/contiguouscache.qdoc" lineno="28" documented="true" subtype="example" title="Contiguous Cache Example" fulltitle="Contiguous Cache Example" subtitle="" module="QtCore" brief="Contiguous Cache example shows how to use QContiguousCache to manage memory usage for very large models. In some environments memory is limited and, even when it isn't, users still dislike an application using excessive memory. Using QContiguousCache to manage a list, rather than loading the entire list into memory, allows the application to limit the amount of memory it uses, regardless of the size of the data set it accesses">
